        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac16$\n\nAverage the three within-school probabilities.",
          "worked": "The schools are equally likely. Within the chosen school, multiply its gum-chewing probability by itself.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{both})&=\\frac13\\left(0.50^2+0.40^2+0.30^2\\right)\\\\P(\\text{both})&=\\frac13(0.25+0.16+0.09)\\\\P(\\text{both})&=\\frac16.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-p1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "only one of those students chews gum.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac7{15}$\n\nCount both orders in each school, then average the three probabilities.",
          "worked": "In a school with gum-chewing probability $p$, each order has probability $p(1-p)$, so the probability of exactly one is $2p(1-p)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{exactly one})&=\\frac{2}{3}\\left(0.50\\times0.50+0.40\\times0.60+0.30\\times0.70\\right)\\\\P(\\text{exactly one})&=\\frac{2}{3}(0.25+0.24+0.21)\\\\P(\\text{exactly one})&=\\frac7{15}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      }
    ]
  },
